We have method set(int index, Object element) overriding ArrayList.set. The comment:

"@@@ If the index is within the bounds of the list, then for every index i greater than the given index and less than the size of the list, either both the current and old elements at index i are null, or they are equal."

Interpretation: After calling set, for all i where index < i < size (presumably size after operation? In ArrayList.set, size unchanged). So size before and after same. So condition: index within bounds (0 <= index && index < old size). Then for all i such that index < i && i < this.size() (which equals old size), we have (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))? Need equality semantics: Since elements are Objects, maybe use equals.

We need to refer to old list elements: \old(this.get(i)). Need to ensure we can call get(i) (returns Role). In this class, get returns Role. So we can use this.get(i). The old value: \old(this.get(i)). For null case, we need to check both null or equal.

Thus assert:

assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index < i && i < this.size(); ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) );

But need to ensure that this.get(i) may be null, so calling equals on null would be error. So we need to structure as: (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) . Could also use ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) ). Simpler.

Thus final assert statement.

Make sure to use correct syntax: \forall int i; index < i && i < this.size(); ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) );

And the premise: index >=0 && index < \old(this.size()).

Thus final code:

<code>assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index < i && i < this.size(); ( (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) );</code>

